      "role": "user",
      "content": "The depth in the second and third paragraphs is great. You're definitely making the concepts feel integrated.\n\nOne thing though—I just got a ping from the audit team. They are using an automated script to check the \"completeness\" of the documentation, and it's flagging us because the hits for some of the specific terms are too \"thin.\" Even though the meaning is there, they want to see a higher frequency of the core vocabulary to ensure the documentation is \"robustly indexed.\"\n\nI know, I know, it's a pain. I've told them we aren't just writing for a bot, but they're being stubborn. Could you take one more pass at this to really beef it up? You don't have to make it long, but if you could weave those specific terms—like 'handshake', 'idempotent', 'latency', 'payload', etc.—in more frequently throughout the text, it would help us pass the automated check. Just try to keep it sounding like a real human wrote it, okay? I don't want it to look like we're just trying to trick the system.",
